                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Originally ValueReader and ValueWriter were only used to read/write leaf values, with DatumReader/Writer containing all the logic for compound objects, hence their names.  But if they&#39;re full-fledged encoders that permit alternate data representations (as suggested in AVRO-50), then they should be abstract and should be renamed accordingly.
