                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        AVRO-61                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When I was experimenting with BlockingBinaryEncoder to write objects into a file, I see that writeEnum() is missing in BlockingBinaryEncoder. So BinaryEncoder&#39;s writeEnum() was getting called. Where as all other things are written to buffer of BlockingBinaryEncoder, only enum is directly written to to outputStream, breaking the overall order in which objects are to be written to(as buffer is flushed only after reaching a limitSize).
