</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        AVRO-41,                                                AVRO-109                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hadoop MapReduce performance benefits greatly if data may be compared without deserializing to an object, but rather by examining its serialized bytes directly.  Such &quot;raw&quot; comparators are typically written by hand in Hadoop, and are very fragile.<br/>
<br/>
With Avro it is possible to generically compare two serialized byte sequences if their schema is known.  This should work for any Avro data, regardless of how it was serialized or how it will be deserialized.
  </td>
