                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When reading records out of a file object container using the Python bindings, it would be great to be able to say:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
for record in dfr:<br/>
  &lt;do something with record&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
There&#39;s already a &quot;next()&quot; method defined on the DataFileReader, but the __iter__ method is not defined and we &quot;return None&quot; instead of &quot;raise StopIteration&quot; when out of records.<br/>

  </td>
