                                            <td class="environment">      Java
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Take a look at line 677 in Schema.java<br/>
if (this.containsKey(o)) return this.get(o);<br/>
<br/>
I think this should be super.get(o) but I&#39;m not sure since I have no idea what this method is suppose to do, but it definately recurses infinitly.<br/>
<br/>
    public Names except(final Schema schema) {<br/>
      final Names parent = this;<br/>
      return new Names(space) {<br/>
        public Schema get(Object o) {<br/>
          if (this.containsKey(o)) return this.get(o);<br/>
          if (((NamedSchema)schema).name.equals(o)) return null;<br/>
          return parent.get(o);<br/>
        }<br/>
      };<br/>

  </td>
