</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        AVRO-248                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Because Unions end up deserializing as java.lang.Object and using the object&#39;s type to differentiate the union constituents, object reuse is pretty hard to achieve. I don&#39;t have a specific benchmark, but I think this will hurt performance for logging applications where every record in a large file is a union, and the type tends to change for each record.
