                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Jon Hsieh pointed out that ReflectDatumWriter always returned a DatumWriter&lt;Object&gt;, though it&#39;s often clear (by the way the schema is constructed) that there&#39;s a more specific type that could be used.  In the quote below, the second line would be preferable to the third.<br/>
<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
  Schema schema = reflectData.getSchema(MyObject.class);<br/>
  // DatumWriter&lt;MyObject&gt; writer = new ReflectDatumWriter(schema);<br/>
  DatumWriter&lt;Object&gt; writer = new ReflectDatumWriter(schema);<br/>
{noformat}
  </td>
