                                            <td class="environment">      OpenJDK 1.6, Linux
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      It is possible to crash an avro rpc server (java) by writing random strings to the socket:<br/>
<br/>
Try... <br/>
echo &quot;boom&quot; | nc localhost 9160<br/>
<br/>
You get...<br/>
java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space<br/>
	at java.nio.HeapByteBuffer.&lt;init&gt;(HeapByteBuffer.java:57)<br/>
	at java.nio.ByteBuffer.allocate(ByteBuffer.java:329)<br/>
	at org.apache.avro.ipc.SocketTransceiver.readBuffers(SocketTransceiver.java:65)<br/>
	at org.apache.avro.ipc.SocketServer$Connection.run(SocketServer.java:91)<br/>
	at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:636)
  </td>
