                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Like sources, javadoc should be generated and published via maven.<br/>
<br/>
This means that in IDE&#39;s like Eclipse use of the Avro APIs will have handy javadoc tooltips and auto-complete options will contain javadoc.   Also, it is becoming the standard way to distribute javadoc alongside code and source.<br/>
<br/>
I assume, this is done very similarly to AVRO-416.
