                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Upon Scott Banachowski&#39;s request, this is to add HTTP transport support for the rpc usage of avro C++ version. The current implementation uses HTTP POST to send over a request body (of any content) and the server side responds with a standard HTTP response body (of any content). <br/>
<br/>
Current status: it only requires a user to provide a streambuf input and define a function that contains the business logic to generate the serialized content into a response streambuf.  testhttpserver would be a good example there.<br/>

  </td>
