                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      records with the same name as a member generate bad c++ code:<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
{<br/>
    &quot;type&quot; : &quot;array&quot;,<br/>
    &quot;name&quot; : &quot;optionals&quot;,<br/>
    &quot;items&quot; : [<br/>
       { &quot;name&quot; : &quot;l&quot;, &quot;type&quot; : &quot;record&quot;, &quot;fields&quot; : [ { &quot;name&quot; : &quot;l&quot;, &quot;type&quot;: &quot;long&quot;} ] },<br/>
       { &quot;name&quot; : &quot;r&quot;, &quot;type&quot; : &quot;record&quot;, &quot;fields&quot; : [ { &quot;name&quot; : &quot;r&quot;, &quot;type&quot;: &quot;long&quot;} ] }<br/>
    ]<br/>
}<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
produces c++ code such that when it is compiled it produces:<br/>
<br/>
union2.h:42: error: field &#39;int64_t avrouser::l::l&#39; with same name as class<br/>

