                <tr id="issuerow12464467" rel="12464467" data-issuekey="AVRO-540" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-540" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-540">AVRO-540</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                make GenericArray reversible
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Eric Evans
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Eric Evans
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Eric Evans
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 13/May/10 21:01 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 08/Sep/10 21:07 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 13/May/10 21:56 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.3.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.4.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      There are a number of RPC methods in Cassandra that return ordered results (ordered by pluggable comparators, avro&#39;s ordering won&#39;t work), and each has a means of specifying that the order be reversed. The way this is currently done is to use a List to process the results, Collections.reverse() to reorder if needed, and then copy them to a GenericArray to be returned. It would be nice to avoid this intermediary step.<br/>
<br/>
The patch that follows adds a reverse() method to GenericData.Array that simply reverses the order of the elements in the underlying Object[].<br/>

  </td>
