                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently, test_tools.sh will fail if the JAVA_HOME environment variable is not set, even if there is a java on the PATH. I generally trust Philip on testing, but I&#39;ve been bitten a few times by this requirement while trying to build a release. It&#39;s low priority, but if it doesn&#39;t violate anyone&#39;s test-related sensibilities, I&#39;d love to have this test just run with the first &quot;java&quot; it finds on the path if JAVA_HOME is not set.
