</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I have a use-case where I need to write serialized classes to a stream, and the reader of the stream may not have those classes.  In such a case, I would like the reader to be able to invoke DataFileReader#invoke within a try{} block to catch the AvroRuntimeException(ClassNotFoundException) and move on.<br/>
<br/>
This currently does not work, because of an exception thrown when retrieving a Symbol.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve attached a test which demonstrates this problem.
  </td>
