                <tr id="issuerow12470296" rel="12470296" data-issuekey="AVRO-601" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-601" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-601">AVRO-601</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Enhance schema parser to allow arbitrary properties to be defined on a record field
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Doug Cutting
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            David Rosenstrauch
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            David Rosenstrauch
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Jul/10 21:08 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 08/Sep/10 21:08 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 03/Aug/10 22:50 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.4.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java,                     spec            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      All
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      It&#39;s currently not possible to add an arbitrary property on a record field.  e.g., in the following example, although the schema parses fine, the &quot;alias&quot; property gets thrown away:<br/>
<br/>
{<br/>
    &quot;name&quot;: &quot;KVPair&quot;,<br/>
    &quot;type&quot;: &quot;record&quot;,<br/>
    &quot;fields&quot; : [<br/>
        {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;key&quot;, &quot;type&quot;: &quot;int&quot;, &quot;alias&quot;: &quot;EventTime&quot;},<br/>
        {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;values&quot;, &quot;type&quot;: &quot;bytes&quot;}<br/>
    ]<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
I had read the Avro spec and thought this was actually allowed (&quot;Attributes not defined in this document are permitted as metadata, but must not affect the format of serialized data.&quot;) but it appears that such additional properties are only allowed at the schema level, not at the field level too.<br/>
<br/>
This would be a really useful feature to have, as it would allow the user to define meta-data on a field.  Currently the only other way to achieve the same behavior would be to do some kind of hack using the field&#39;s &quot;doc&quot; attribute, which would be rather ugly. 
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
