    </td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Ubuntu 10.04 amd64, github checkout
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Here&#39;s a sample of what I did to repro the bug:<br/>
&gt; git clone git://github.com/apache/avro.git<br/>
&gt; cd avro<br/>
&gt; ./build.sh dist<br/>
+ for target in &#39;&quot;$@&quot;&#39;<br/>
+ case &quot;$target&quot; in<br/>
+ mkdir -p build<br/>
+ rm -rf build/avro-src-1.4.0-SNAPSHOT<br/>
+ svn export --force . build/avro-src-1.4.0-SNAPSHOT<br/>
svn: &#39;.&#39; is not a working copy<br/>
<br/>
the hack solution would probably to check for the existence of diretories .svn or .git and execute the appropriate command.
  </td>
