                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        AVRO-641,                                                HTTPCLIENT-523                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      [SPNEGO|http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SPNEGO] is the standard mechanism for Kerberos authentication over HTTP. <br/>
<br/>
Avro should give users the option of using an Avro HTTP client or server that is capable of authentication using SPNEGO/Kerberos. This will be useful for Hadoop which has chosen Kerberos as its standard authentication protocol, as well as people who need to use Kerberos authentication with Avro based services running in servlet containers like Tomcat.<br/>
<br/>
References:<br/>
* [LGPL licensed SPNEGO library for Java|http://spnego.sourceforge.net/]<br/>
* [Glassfish Spnego project|https://spnego.dev.java.net/]<br/>
* [SPNEGO authentication scheme for HTTPClient|https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/HTTPCLIENT-523]<br/>

  </td>
