</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      DataFileReader.blockStart is hidden from the caller, but exposing it (as readonly) would allow callers to discover sync points in a file by watching it for changes.<br/>
<br/>
seek(long) only takes an exact block boundary, while sync(long) moves to the next block boundary. There does not appear to be a way to rediscover points that you can seek() to, which would be very useful for building or recovering an index for a file.
  </td>
