                <tr id="issuerow12477168" rel="12477168" data-issuekey="AVRO-680" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-680" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-680">AVRO-680</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Allow for non-string keys
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sachin Goyal
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jeremy Hanna
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jeremy Hanna
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 12/Oct/10 18:37 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 28/Jun/17 02:43 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 15/Mar/15 03:30 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.6,                     1.7.7            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.8.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">5</td>
                                            <td class="watches">11</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Based on an email thread back in April, Doug Cutting proposed a possible solution for having non-string keys:<br/>
<br/>
Stu Hood wrote:<br/>
&gt; I can understand the reasoning behind AVRO-9, but now I need to look for an alternative to a &#39;map&#39; that will allow me to store an association of bytes keys to values.<br/>
<br/>
A map of Foo has the same binary format as an array of records, each<br/>
with a string field and a Foo field.  So an application can use an array<br/>
schema similar to this to represent map-like structures with, e.g.,<br/>
non-string keys.<br/>
<br/>
Perhaps we could establish standard properties that indicate that a<br/>
given array of records should be represented in a map-like way if<br/>
possible?  E.g.,:<br/>
<br/>
{&quot;type&quot;: &quot;array&quot;, &quot;isMap&quot;: true, &quot;items&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;:&quot;record&quot;, ...}}<br/>
<br/>
Doug
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
