    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 19/Nov/10 21:48 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 12/Mar/11 00:32 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 22/Nov/10 06:18 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.4.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.5.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 2003 Server
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Emprty name for a type in .avro file creates java class with compile-time errors.<br/>
<br/>
Try to generate  java object for the following avro defintion.<br/>
<br/>
{<br/>
&quot;namespace&quot; : &quot;com.ebay.test.benchmark.avro&quot;,<br/>
&quot;protocol&quot;: &quot;AvroBenchmarkProtocol&quot;,<br/>
&quot;doc&quot;: &quot;BenchmarkingAvro&quot;,<br/>
