                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        AVRO-770,                                                AVRO-839                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently, GenericDatumReader/GenericDatumWriter data members are private. Is it possible to make them protected so that we could extend those classes and create our own special DatumReader/Writer? The reason we want to do that is because we&#39;ve created our own base SpecificRecordEx that implements SpecificRecord and added put/get for primitive types. We now want to extend the GenericDatumReader/GenericDatumWriter to use those primitive put/get functions to reduce box/unbox for better performance. <br/>
Thanks,<br/>
<br/>
Xiaolu
  </td>
