                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The avro_bytes_set function (and its string and fixed counterparts) are supposed to save a copy of the value, which the avro_datum_t instance takes full control over.  Unfortunately, we were making that copy but then saving the original pointer, which would lead to a segfault when freeing the datum.  Whoops...
