</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Snappy-Java 1.0.3.1 adds the capability of disabling of loading the in-JAR native library and isntead loading it from the java.library.path.<br/>
<br/>
The version of Snappy-Java currently used by Avro (1.0.3-rc4) does not allow this in-jAR native library disabling.<br/>
<br/>
This capability enables the use of a native library built in the target platform (some versions of Linux -stable ones- fail to work with the generic Linux SO file bundled in Snappy-Java).<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
