</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      N/A
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      We have switched over to the new value_t API for our application, as it provides more AVRO types that we need (enum, array, etc), however we have noticed that there isn&#39;t a way to write out a spec compatible AVRO file.<br/>
<br/>
The old API was able to write out a header as well as the schema, the finally each data block (and sync marker).<br/>
<br/>
I could possibly try and re-implement this myself, however I am unsure as to the design (how it would fit into the new datum API).
