</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The problems are:<br/>
1. The executable filename is passed around as a URL. Windows filenames are valid URLs.<br/>
2. Typical windows user&#39;s home directory is {{c:\Documents and Settings\username}}. Maven puts the downloaded jar files under {{$HOME/.m2}}. So the classpath has several directories with space in their names. Splitting command line arguments using space generates invalid classpath.<br/>
3. Hadoop&#39;s {{TaskLog.captureOutAndError()}} generates command line for unix systems using bash. 
  </td>
