                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      On Mac OS X, you need to use install_name_tool to set the install_name property for any shared libraries, especially if they&#39;re installed into a non standard location.  The CMake scripts don&#39;t do this by default:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
$ otool -D /tmp/foobar/lib/libavro.22.0.0.dylib <br/>
/tmp/foobar/lib/libavro.22.0.0.dylib:<br/>
libavro.22.0.0.dylib<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
This means that anything that links with libavro can&#39;t find the library at runtime.
  </td>
