                <tr id="issuerow12534307" rel="12534307" data-issuekey="AVRO-972" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-972" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-972">AVRO-972</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Avro IDL compiler should support &quot;NaN&quot;, &quot;Infinity&quot;, and &quot;-Infinity&quot; as float literals
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Doug Cutting
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Brandon Ballinger
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Brandon Ballinger
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/Dec/11 06:19 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 15/Feb/12 00:46 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 09/Dec/11 20:27 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.6.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.6.2            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The Avro IDL defines floating point literals as follows:<br/>
  &lt; FLOATING_POINT_LITERAL:<br/>
  (&quot;-&quot;)?<br/>
    ( &lt;DECIMAL_FLOATING_POINT_LITERAL&gt; | &lt;HEXADECIMAL_FLOATING_POINT_LITERAL&gt; )<br/>
  &gt;<br/>
|<br/>
  &lt; #DECIMAL_FLOATING_POINT_LITERAL:<br/>
        ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;])+ &quot;.&quot; ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;])* (&lt;DECIMAL_EXPONENT&gt;)? ([&quot;f&quot;,&quot;F&quot;,&quot;d&quot;,&quot;D&quot;])?<br/>
      | &quot;.&quot; ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;])+ (&lt;DECIMAL_EXPONENT&gt;)? ([&quot;f&quot;,&quot;F&quot;,&quot;d&quot;,&quot;D&quot;])?<br/>
      | ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;])+ &lt;DECIMAL_EXPONENT&gt; ([&quot;f&quot;,&quot;F&quot;,&quot;d&quot;,&quot;D&quot;])?<br/>
      | ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;])+ (&lt;DECIMAL_EXPONENT&gt;)? [&quot;f&quot;,&quot;F&quot;,&quot;d&quot;,&quot;D&quot;]<br/>
  &gt;<br/>
|<br/>
  &lt; #DECIMAL_EXPONENT: [&quot;e&quot;,&quot;E&quot;] ([&quot;+&quot;,&quot;-&quot;])? ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;])+ &gt;<br/>
|<br/>
  &lt; #HEXADECIMAL_FLOATING_POINT_LITERAL:<br/>
        &quot;0&quot; [&quot;x&quot;, &quot;X&quot;] ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;,&quot;a&quot;-&quot;f&quot;,&quot;A&quot;-&quot;F&quot;])+ (&quot;.&quot;)? &lt;HEXADECIMAL_EXPONENT&gt; ([&quot;f&quot;,&quot;F&quot;,&quot;d&quot;,&quot;D&quot;])?<br/>
      | &quot;0&quot; [&quot;x&quot;, &quot;X&quot;] ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;,&quot;a&quot;-&quot;f&quot;,&quot;A&quot;-&quot;F&quot;])* &quot;.&quot; ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;,&quot;a&quot;-&quot;f&quot;,&quot;A&quot;-&quot;F&quot;])+ &lt;HEXADECIMAL_EXPONENT&gt; ([&quot;f&quot;,&quot;F&quot;,&quot;d&quot;,&quot;D&quot;])?<br/>
  &gt;<br/>
|<br/>
  &lt; #HEXADECIMAL_EXPONENT: [&quot;p&quot;,&quot;P&quot;] ([&quot;+&quot;,&quot;-&quot;])? ([&quot;0&quot;-&quot;9&quot;])+ &gt;<br/>
<br/>
Java allows for &quot;NaN&quot;, &quot;Infinity&quot;, and &quot;-Infinity&quot; when parsing a Double from a String:<br/>
  http://docs.oracle.com/javase/6/docs/api/java/lang/Double.html#valueOf(java.lang.String)<br/>
<br/>
The IDL compiler should allow the same set of values as Java Double.valueOf. Among other things, this would allow &quot;NaN&quot; to be used as a default value for float fields in Avro records.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
