</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      {noformat}<br/>
Tests run: 4, Failures: 1, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0, Time elapsed: 15.554 sec &lt;&lt;&lt; FAILURE!<br/>
testTonsOfSpans(org.apache.avro.ipc.trace.TestFileSpanStorage)  Time elapsed: 3.853 sec  &lt;&lt;&lt; FAILURE!<br/>
java.lang.AssertionError: expected:&lt;50000&gt; but was:&lt;42356&gt;<br/>
        at org.junit.Assert.fail(Assert.java:93)<br/>
        at org.junit.Assert.failNotEquals(Assert.java:647)<br/>
        at org.junit.Assert.assertEquals(Assert.java:128)<br/>
        at org.junit.Assert.assertEquals(Assert.java:472)<br/>
        at org.junit.Assert.assertEquals(Assert.java:456)<br/>
        at org.apache.avro.ipc.trace.TestFileSpanStorage.testTonsOfSpans(TestFileSpanStorage.java:70)<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
<br/>
The issue seems to be the {{Thread.sleep(2000)}} on line 66.  Doubling this to 4000ms causes the test to pass.  In general it might be better to make this sleep event-based rather than using a fixed sleep time.  If that isn&#39;t possible, then maybe using some sort of a retry loop would work.
  </td>
